  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Flood Disaster in Ethiopia, Somalia, and Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2023 deyr (October to December) rain season has resulted in heavy rainfall and flooding across Somalia, exacerbated by El Ni&#xf1;o and a positive Indian Ocean Dipole in the region, particularly in Puntland, Galmudug, South-West, Hirshabelle and Jubaland states. The floods have inundated farmlands, destroyed roads and bridges, and cut off access to towns and villages for displaced people, also impacting the access for humanitarian action to the most affected areas. Through this project, IOM is providing emergency assistance to individuals affected and displaced due to flooding caused by El Ni&#xf1;o in Somalia. The focus is on delivering emergency shelter support and rehabilitating damaged shelters to ensure the safety and well-being of the affected population.</narrative>
  </description>
